# `onstart` handler below, not here at parse time. Snakemake only fires
# `onstart` when a run actually begins executing jobs — never on dry-run,
# unlock, --dag, --list, env pre-build, and the like. That keeps the banner
# tied to a genuine run without having to enumerate every administrative
# invocation that merely parses the workflow.

